Z||000010||BENGAL4||01-17-2000||03:05 PM||||Gokart,<P>You need a 10mm & 8mm, 12 point sockets. You can get them @ Autozone. I repainted my plenum and valve covers this summer. Good luck. ||||reg||14
Z||000011||David Gamache||01-17-2000||06:42 PM||||The two long black torks bolts that hold the throtle body use a #40 bit. Unless your bolts are damaged it should work.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Gokart||01-17-2000||06:46 PM||||Thanks Bengal4, but like I said above I have those sockets. This is not for the bolts going into the manifold. It's for the two rounded screws that go from the throttle body to the plenum. Your right David. Thanks. Bought a T-40 bit today and planned on grinding it to fit so I tried it to see how much I was going to have to grind off and it slipped right in! So it's a T-40 after all!! I'm going to that link I posted above and ask them to change it so they don't have another sucker calling 15 hardware stores and 25 autoparts stores looking for T-35!!<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 01-17-2000).]||||reg||4
